course: dictionary
lesson: 2195
title: Cougar: a big wild cat with many names
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some animals have more than one name, and a text may give you the second name as a clue. «Pumas, also called cougars or mountain lions, chirp, hiss, purr and scream but cannot roar.» The words «also called» tell you that puma, cougar and mountain lion are all names for the same animal.
explain: Be careful with names that look like other words. A mountain lion is not a lion, even though it has lion in its name. The sentence says so: «a mountain lion is not a lion.» When a name seems to mislead you, check the rest of the text.
explain: A cougar is a large wild cat with brown fur and a long tail. You can test your meaning by swapping it into a sentence: «The cougar crept through the forest» still makes sense if you think of a big wild cat, so your meaning fits.
fact: A cougar is a large wild cat of North and South America.
fact: Cougars have brown fur and a long tail.
fact: A cougar is also called a puma or a mountain lion.
fact: Cougars cannot roar, but they can chirp, hiss, purr and scream.
fact: Cougars live in mountains and forests, from Canada to Chile, and they hunt deer. They are mostly shy of people.
exercise: «Pumas, also called cougars or mountain lions, chirp, hiss, purr and scream.» What do the words «also called» tell you? | A cougar is a small bird | *A cougar is another name for a puma | A cougar is a kind of dog | A cougar lives under the sea
exercise: You are in cougar country and you see one. What should you do? | Run as fast as you can | Lie down on the ground and hide | *Stay in a group, stand tall and make noise | Walk right up to it to take a photo
exercise: «Pumas, also called cougars or mountain lions, chirp, hiss, purr and scream but cannot roar.» Which sound can a cougar NOT make? | *Roar | Chirp | Hiss | Purr
test: Where do cougars live? | In the cold seas of the Arctic | In the deserts of Africa | *In the mountains and forests of the Americas | In the cities of Europe
test: What do cougars hunt? | Eggs from birds' nests | *Deer | Fish from rivers | Grass and leaves
exam: Mia says a cougar must be a kind of lion because its name has lion in it. Who is right? | *Mia is wrong, because a mountain lion is not a lion, and a cougar is a big wild cat with brown fur | Mia is right, because it is a small pet | Mia is right, because it is a lion from Africa
